     would be a /cart.js request a second on every page of the site. The lines
     are fingerprinted from the DOM instead (variant x quantity, no request) and
     /cart.js is only fetched when that fingerprint moves or the drawer says the
     cart changed. Everything else a mutation can need -- the cards put back
     after a rebuild, the pictures re-checked -- is done from what the last
     read left behind. */
  var reading = false, again = false, timer = null, seenSig = null;
  /* THE DRAWER MUST SHOW WHAT /cart.js HOLDS (2026-09-21, owner: "it's not
